WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:04.871
 Julien, JW, it's come down
to France and the United States

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.607
in our first ever
international competition.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.375
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:12.144
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.512
Are you ready to see what it is?

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:14.980
 Not ready.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:16.416
 Well, that weapon is--

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.419
the spadroon.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.522
All right, bladesmiths.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:24.323
Good luck.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.825
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.562 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:34.000
JULIEN: I'm happy to
be home in France.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:37.370
Look at the nice view behind us.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.838
It's magnificent.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.709
So I start to make my tip,
but I have to be really fast.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:48.814
Because more you hit your
blade, less carbon you have.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.116
[clanking]

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.717
it's like music.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:52.952
[french] music.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.088
I love to do some
music with my hammer.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.121
(SINGING) Dum, dum, pick it up.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.091
Dum, dum, pick it up.

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.193
It just gets you some rhythm.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.661
It's just more fun.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.767
Today I did it all--

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.568
turned the tip, the blade.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:13.906
All I have left is to
grind it a little bit.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:17.476
And it's going very well.

00:01:17.576 --> 00:01:18.678
Boom!

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.080 line:8%
JW: Well, I'm excited to
get started this morning.

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:22.682
Fixing to start
profiling everything,

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:26.252
so I'm going to spend a bunch
of time at the grinder today.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.687
With the length of
this blade, I mean,

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.089
it's like grinding three
10-inch Bowie knives.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.357
You've got a ton of work.

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.530
Just getting everything
rough ground out.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.331
We're just about ready to
go to heat treat on it,

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.868
so right now would be
time for a little prayer.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.637
Now, the grinding process was
slower than I would have liked

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.139
for it to be, so this
is a short amount

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.775
of time left to heat treat.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.810
[music playing]

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.114
[torch]

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:06.292
I notice this curve from the top
down, and it just heart sinks.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.262
I've got to do something
to correct this.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.830
I know I can't fix it cold,
so we've got to go back in

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.200
and heat treat again.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.335
I take it out of the oil
and I got that same thing.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.405
And I'm thinking I'm going
have to regroup and start over.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.308 line:8%
JULIEN: So today,
I'm going to work

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:25.344
to be ready for the quench.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:29.415
The quench is important because
if the quench is not good,

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.183
my blade's going
to be like butter,

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:35.555
and she's going to
bend at the first shot.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.557
[music playing]

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.797
I think it bent.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.399
Oh, [bleep].

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:50.202
I know that there's a weak point
on my blade to make the curve,

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:52.104
so I have to do a second one.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.374
[music playing]

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.316
[burning]

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:06.085
[whistle]

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.587
Boom.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.889
Third quench.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.991
This one goes down, I don't
want to do another one.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.195
[music playing]

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:20.767
[whistle]

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.102
We have to make another blade.

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:24.570 line:14%
I have to restart everything.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.504
[clanking]

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.839
I don't want to
do another blade.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.375
But I've got my
country behind me,

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.044
so I have to show
them that I respect

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.046
them, and give the best.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.416 line:14%
Yeah.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.951
 I thought about a lot,
what happened yesterday.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.419
I've got plenty to work with.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:43.356
But I still got a slight
curve in the spine,

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:46.758
so what I'm going to have
to do is grind that away.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.828
[music playing]

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.131
Going good.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:55.300
As I'm grinding, I can tell that
this thing is going to be OK.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.137
What a huge relief that is.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.139 line:8%
And now that this
plate issue is fixed,

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.874
I can focus on fit and finish.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:05.277
What's challenging about it is
hitting the sizing right on it.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.612
Instead of having
a round handle,

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.481
we're going to have
an oval handle.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.316
There's just nothing
comfortable about a round

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.785
handle when you're striking
something on an angle.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.320
Done deal.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.288
I've got real high
expectations of it.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:17.289
I really do.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:19.659
I think it's going to do well.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.027
 Bladesmiths, to find out
how lethal your weapons are,

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:25.364
I will deliver some slashes and
thrusts on these big carcasses.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.799
Julien, you're up first.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:27.566
You ready?

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:28.534
 I think so.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.335
[laughing]

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.537
[music playing]

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.541
[slashing]

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:52.925
All right, Julien, let's
talk about your sword here.

00:04:52.991 --> 00:04:54.727
It's a bit on the heavier side.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:59.098
Your edge easily lacerates
into the big carcass.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.567
On the thrust, it
penetrates deep.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.836
Your weapon definitely is sharp.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.804
Your sword will kill.

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:06.939
 Thank you.

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:07.974
 JW, you're next.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:08.741
You ready?

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.976
 Think so.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.011
[music playing]

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:14.047
[slashing]

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.132
 OK, JW.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.967
Let's talk about
your spadroon, here.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:37.369
The fact that you put a fuller
all the way through up here

00:05:37.469 --> 00:05:39.237
lightened your sword a lot.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.107
It is so sharp,
it almost cut all

00:05:42.207 --> 00:05:43.609
the way through this carcass.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:46.713
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.081
 Thank you, Doug.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.949
 Now, Donald McBane, who
wrote the book on this weapon,

00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:52.485
called it the shearing sword.

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.252
So to test the sharpness
of your blades,

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.721
I'll be chopping
through this rope,

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:58.424
and then attacking these
sandbags as they fall.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:05:59.791
Julien you're up.
Are you ready?

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:00.593
 Oui.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.895
 OK.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.162
[slashing]

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.598
[music playing]

00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:07.433
 Whew!

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:11.671
 I'll get him.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.773
[slashing]

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:18.010
[music playing]

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:21.347
[sand spilling]

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.749
JULIEN: Yes.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:24.317
It's good.

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.251
 Good job.

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.185
 It's breaking good.

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:30.122
 Well, Julien, that's sharp.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.724
It passed right
through the ropes.

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.893
It passed right
through the bags.

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:37.597
But the weight in this sword,
and the shape of its handle,

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:42.201
just have a tendency to
be very hard to stop.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.369
A little thinner
handle, possibly.

00:06:44.436 --> 00:06:45.171
A little more indexed--

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.071
JULIEN: Yeah.

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.206
 --would have helped.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.974
But it's definitely
a sharp sword.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:50.543
 Thank you very much.

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:52.678
Sir, you are next.

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:53.245
Are you ready?

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.848
 Yes, sir.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.215
[slashing]

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.552
[music playing]

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:05.425
[sand spilling]

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:25.511
 Definitely sharp enough
to cut through the ropes.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.780
Your handle, would have
been nice to see it taper

00:07:27.846 --> 00:07:31.116
and swell a little bit more,
but it's definitely a cutter.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:32.084
 Thank you.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:33.319
DAVID BAKER: Nicely done.

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:34.353
All right, gentlemen.

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:35.921
Next up is the strength test.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.923
Now, to test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.026
I'll be thrusting with the
tip and cutting these hardwood

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:42.294
leather-wrapped shields.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:44.163
JW, you ready for this?

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:44.997
 Yes, sir.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:45.764
[music playing]

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.800
[chopping]

00:07:59.711 --> 00:08:02.214
 Well, everything on
the blade looks good.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.215
Guard's still tight.

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.483
Handle hasn't moved.

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:05.450
I think you did a great job.

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.319
 Thank you, Dave.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.755
 Julien, are you ready?

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:10.789
 Good luck.

00:08:10.856 --> 00:08:12.558
[chopping]

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.760
[music playing]

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:28.974
 So, Julien, you've got
a very stout edge profile.

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:30.142
Blade's still straight.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:31.077
Well done.

00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:32.111
 Thank you so much.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:35.848
 Well, gentlemen.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.716
The judges have
made their decision.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:41.987
Our very first "Forged in Fire"
International Champion is JW.

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:45.357
Congratulations, you are
our first "Forged In Fire"

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:47.225
International Champion.

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:48.060
Julien--

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.462
 Oui?

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:52.531
 Unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:54.032
J. Neilson will explain.

00:08:54.132 --> 00:08:57.737 line:8%
J. NEILSON: Julien, you
brought us a beautiful piece.

00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:01.040 line:8%
But compared to your competitor,
your blade was a lot heavier

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.508 line:14%
in the front, balance-wise.

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:04.276 line:8%
And with that round
handle, it made it a lot

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:05.877 line:14%
harder control in the testing.

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:08.280
That's why we're
going to let you go.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.582
 Julien, say finis, mon ami.

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:12.652
Please surrender your weapon.

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:13.553
 OK.

00:09:16.488 --> 00:09:17.689
 Thank you, guys.

00:09:17.756 --> 00:09:23.261
I'm very proud of this
blade, but JW's a god.

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:27.433
He's a god in the forge.

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:30.102
And this guy is my friend.

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:36.342
 JW, the American, and
our very first "Forged

00:09:36.408 --> 00:09:38.210
in Fire" International Champion.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:41.980
It's a title that also comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:43.149
Congratulations.

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:45.784
Please present your
weapon to the judges.

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:49.989
 I put forth a lot of
hard work, time, and effort

00:09:50.056 --> 00:09:51.090
to reach this point.

00:09:51.156 --> 00:09:53.893
So it's just been an
incredible honor to be

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:55.727
asked to represent my country.

00:09:55.794 --> 00:09:57.830
And not only that, but
being able to meet guys

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.599
from different parts of the
world, and the friendships

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:03.502
that we developed, was
just a great experience.

00:10:03.568 --> 00:10:04.536
And that's what it's all about.

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:07.139
[music playing]

